title Caravan lapse -- an objection is put back to its reader, and answered or let go
prompt Kyri first, then REMEMBER and the road-ahead itineraries; Standfast on reds, then the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; council rota one doc; condense REMEMBER when a set closes; send each finished increment
think Standfast first. The living REDS ledger reads five rows and every one closed -- %96 and %97 both released with witnesses on metal last lap. No open agent-closable red stands, so the constructive queue opens honestly.
think The running thread is the Caravan correction arc, and the newest recommend named the next question exactly: what a run owes a disagreement that never resolves at all -- a mark says somebody objects, and says nothing about how long that objection may stand or what a plan does when the reader who made it never writes again.
think Council rota, lap index 64 mod 27 = 10: deep-read foundations/20260703-182612_sameness-is-the-macro.md. Its principle governed the shape of this lap directly. The escort layer arrived as a second copy of abide's folds; sameness says compress by making things publicly similar, so every pure fold of the rung below became a delegating wrapper and only this rung's own supervisor step stayed local. Learning one rung is learning sixty-five.
think The rung the question wants is a term. An objection recorded once escorts every future read of that word, and nothing ever asks whether the person who raised it still holds it -- so a plan carries a live quarrel long after there is anybody left to have it. The answer is to ask, once, on the wire, and publish what came back.
think The hard half named itself while designing the refusals. A lapse is honest for exactly one reason: its reader was asked again and said nothing. A run that publishes a lapse without ever putting the question back is calling silence an answer it never waited for -- nobody went quiet where nobody was addressed. That became LapseUnasked, and the asking is read back out of the reader's own box before a word of the answer is weighed.
obs The measurement is objections published with no term on them at all. Every rung below weighs a record against a reader's answer or the place a person reads; this one is the first that weighs a record against the life of the person who wrote it. It falls 1 to 0.
obs A term reports, and never withdraws. The escort in plan.beside stays exactly as written when the objection lapses, since a run that erased the mark because its reader went quiet would be winning the quarrel by outlasting them. The wire proves it: the mark still reads s afterward.
obs Both answers the question admits are proven on the wire rather than only as folds. The two-run lap measures the silence; a third run over a reader who raises their objection again in their own hand publishes renewed, so plan.term ends the lap reading r. The witness names why that final byte is the third run's word rather than the finding's.
obs Silence belongs to the person who is silent. renew_as_reader carries the same restraint answer_as_reader does -- no run of this plan ever calls it, because a renewal a supervisor could write for its reader renews nothing at all.
obs Five RED paths proven on metal before any GREEN claim. The fifth is the one worth naming: with the asking, its refusal, and the harness read that catches it all disarmed at once, the run published an objection let go by a reader who was never addressed -- desk.again never written, the question fabricated from the plan's own record, and the selftest still calling itself GREEN. Seeing that once is what makes the asking a check rather than decoration.
obs The compiler stayed quiet this lap, and the tier shift went clean on the first build. What the sameness doc predicted held: a rung publicly similar to the sixty-four below it costs one layer to add rather than one module to write.
obs Registered the rung in the choir in the same round, per REDS %81's lesson. The Caravan choir now sings 65 per-rung witnesses in one voice, roster bijection whole, and caravan/.lapsings joined the ignore roster beside its siblings.
loom witness=caravan_lapse_witness rungs_in_choir=65 phases=6 dependents=6 absorbed=3 abandoned=3 reseated=3 asked_perpetual=0 asked_bounded=1 lapsed_bounded=1 renewed_third_run=1 unbounded_before=1 unbounded_after=0
file caravan/lapse.rye the rung -- a term put on the objection standing beside a published word, asked in the reader's own box and answered in one byte
file tools/caravan_lapse_witness.rish the witness -- five RED paths named, the two-run measurement, the renewal proven on the same wire
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish the choir roster grows to 65, bijection whole
file caravan/README.md the module table row and the rung's own durable section
file .gitignore caravan/.lapsings joins the run-notes ignore roster
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge moves to this rung; the prior edge condenses to a pointer
recommend keep-going the arc has answered for reach at every moment of a dependent's life, repaired what a fall cost, taken back its own stale judgments, written to the reader those judgments misled, carried the letter, read the answer, recorded the disagreement, stood the published word beside it, and now puts a term on how long that objection may stand -- so the question above it is what a run owes an objection it let go: the record still holds both readings and the escort still stands, which is honest and entirely silent about whether a word let go should keep escorting every operator who reads it afterward.
